  "limitations": [
    "Current and parent SDK both failed the phone-to-laptop 4-MiB and 32-MiB 180-second observation window. The managed starvation fix is not sufficient to close cellular completion failures.",
    "Current SDK completed laptop-to-phone 4 MiB in 14.963 s and 32 MiB in 124.497 s. These sequential WAN runs do not isolate a speed benefit.",
    "The separately labeled 60-second trace capture completed 4 MiB phone-to-laptop in 48.414 s after a manifest-phase retry. It does not erase the two failed 180-second gates.",
    "Inclusive reset/attempt counts retain final harness cancellation. Parent small-file control also records a source payload-write-idle timeout.",
    "Resume request offsets are extracted from request-sent resume= logs, not from a resume point recorded only after final cancellation. A queued resume request does not certify server receipt or final integrity.",
    "The ordered-transport samples do not identify the underlying IP transport or prove packet loss/high ping. Local stage maxima concern different observations and must not be summed.",
    "Sampled driver blocked_age measures pending outbound handoff, including cold route opens; it is distinct from the ready-inbound queue delay fixed by this patch.",
    "No calls, audio playout, live speech, Windows execution or full multi-device campaign ran. Reliable-stream ACKs here are not a measurement of audio RTCP behavior."
  ],
